#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asymptotic_equal

#% text
# `asymptotic_equal(f, g, x -> a)` gives true when f and g are of the same order as x approaches a: f = O(g) and g = O(f).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Decided by the upper limits of |f/g| and |g/f|; options `direction:` and `assumptions:` as for `asymptotic_less_equal`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asymptotic_equal(x^2 + x*sin(x), 2*x^2 + 5, x -> inf)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
asymptotic_equal(x, -x^2, x -> inf)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `asymptotic_equivalent`, `asymptotic_less_equal`, `asymptotic_greater_equal`
